WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.430
Animals kill, on average,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:06.600
more than 400 people in the
United States each year,

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.290
and the deadliest of them all

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.913
live a lot closer to you
then you might think.

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:15.750
This is where mountain lions roam.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.440
They're considered one
of the most powerful

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.320
predators on the planet.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.380
But they pose little threat to humans,

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.750
killing about one person
every five to 10 years.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.750
They're far more likely to go after prey

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.610
like deer or raccoons.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:32.690
But when it comes to killing,
size isn't everything.

00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:36.260
There are more than 70 species
of scorpion across the US,

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.800
and together they kill
an average of one person

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.980
about every 2 1/2 years.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.420
But none are more dangerous
than the Arizona bark scorpion,

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.500
which lives primarily in
Arizona and New Mexico.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.200
It's one of 30 species worldwide

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.060
that produces venom
toxic enough to be fatal.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:01.060
Next up is perhaps the most
notorious of killers: sharks.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:05.910
Between 2007 and 2018,
there were 920 shark attacks

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:10.280
worldwide, and more than half
of them were in US waters.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:13.700
But thankfully, most shark
attacks aren't fatal.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.350
And, on average, sharks kill Americans

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.250
just once every 1.7 years.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.900
And, actually, there's
another water-loving predator

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.163
that's more deadly.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:29.030
These toothy reptiles range
from Texas to North Carolina

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:32.090
and kill about one person
every year and a half,

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:35.190
most famously a young boy
who was playing near a pond

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.980
at the Disney World hotel in 2016.

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:42.810
But even alligators and
crocodiles are not as deadly as...

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:44.390
bears.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:47.350
In one color or another,
bears range from Alaska

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:49.940
down through much of the
forested United States.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.540
They kill about one to two people a year.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.500
And nearly half of all fatal
wild bear attacks since 1900

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.270
occurred in one of these
six national parks.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:05.100
But even 1,700-pound bears
have nothing on spiders,

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.340
which, taken all together, kill
around seven people a year.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.930
Most of these deaths are likely
linked to just two spiders:

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.990
the black widow and the brown recluse.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.800
That's because they're the
only two spiders in the US

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.360
with venom that's toxic to humans.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.570
You can find black
widows throughout the US,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.150
and the brown recluse is native

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.050
to the Midwest and the South.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.250
These spiders live in
basements, abandoned shoes,

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:34.410
and outside in piles of rocks and wood.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:36.880
And you know what else you can find there?

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.500
Snakes.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.250
The US has about 20
species of venomous snakes,

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:45.460
which live in every state except Alaska.

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.910
Copperheads are the
most likely to bite you

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.950
and live in the
southeastern United States.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:54.400
But you should be most
aware of rattlesnakes,

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.870
like the eastern and western diamondback,

00:02:56.870 --> 00:03:00.720
which are responsible for the
most snake-related deaths.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:05.393
On average, snakes kill as
many as 10 to 15 people a year.

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:09.410
Oh, and if you really hate snakes,

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:12.040
here are the states with
the highest bite rates

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.370
that you'd definitely want to avoid.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.900
Now, if there's anything
scarier than bears,

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.280
spiders and snakes, it's...

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.780
cows?

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:22.830
That's right.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:26.200
Each year, cows kill about 20 people,

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.500
typically by kicking or trampling.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.950
And about three-quarters
of those incidents

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:33.700
are reportedly deliberate attacks.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.900
Of course, you can find cows everywhere,

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.670
and the same goes for the top
three animals on our list.

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.270
Dogs kill about 30 people a year,

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:46.060
most often from attacks that prove fatal,

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:49.970
and pit bulls are responsible
for more than half of them.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.780
Bees and other stinging insects

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.260
kill nearly 100 people per year,

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.230
often by triggering an allergic reaction.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.890
One kind, often called the killer bee,

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:02.500
is especially aggressive.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:05.130
If disturbed, they'll swarm,

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:09.060
and can sting victims
more than 1,000 times.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.800
And, last but not least,
at the top of our list

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.190
is an animal that isn't toxic

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.770
and doesn't generally attack humans.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.070
Deer.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:23.070
Each year, deer cause about
1.3 million car accidents,

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.810
and about 200 of them are fatal,

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.310
though your risk is much
higher in some states,

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.020
like West Virginia.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.440
But taken all together, your odds of dying

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:35.390
from any kind of animal run-in are slim.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:37.600
And when you compare that
to the leading causes

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.190
of death in America, you'll realize

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:43.773
that animals are the
least of your worries.

